\
.\" Dummy definitions of GNU extension macros, in case an-ext.tmac is absent.
.de UR
..
.de UE
.RI \\$1
..
.de MR
.BR "\\$1" "(\\$2)\\$3"
..
\
.TH AXRENOIRSCAN "1" "@PACKAGE_VERSION@" openrenoir
\
.SH NAME
\
axrenoirscan \- generate a preliminary configure.ac and add openrenoir support
\
.SH SYNOPSIS
\
.B axrenoirscan
.RB [ \-\-install ]
.RB [ \-\-install\-acdir
.IR m4-dir ]
.RB [ \-\-install\-auxdir
.IR aux-dir ]
.RI [... autoscan-options ...]
.RI [ src-dir ]
\
.PP
.B axrenoirscan
.RB [ \-h " | " \-? " | " \-\-help " | " \-V " | " \-\-version ]
\
.SH DESCRIPTION
\
.B axrenoirscan
invokes GNU Autoconf's
.MR autoscan 1
to generate a preliminary
.B configure.ac
(as
.BR configure.scan )
for a source code project.
\
.PP
If the project looks for a C macro
.B PACKAGE_CHECK_ABSENT
or
.BR _PACKAGE_CHECK_ABSENT ,
then
.B axrenoirscan
will also add Autoconf macro invocations to compute its value,
and install necessary support files for it.
\
.SH OPTIONS
\
.TP
.B \-\-install
Copy out support files to the project tree.
\
.TP
.BI \-\-install-acdir " m4-dir"
If
.B \-\-install
is specified, install
.B .m4
files in
.IR m4-dir .
\
.TP
.BI \-\-install-auxdir " aux-dir"
If
.B \-\-install
is specified, install to
.IR aux-dir
any additional auxiliary files to be used during
.B configure
time.
\
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-? ", " \-\-help
Display tool usage information and exit.
\
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Display tool version information and exit.
\
.PP
.B axrenoirscan
also recognizes the
.MR autoscan 1
options
.BR \-v ,
.BR \-\-verbose ,
.BR \-d ,
.BR \-\-debug ,
.B \-B
.IR dir ,
.B \-\-prepend\-include
.IR dir ,
.B \-I
.IR dir ,
and
.B \-\-include
.IR dir ,
and passes them to
.MR autoscan 1 .
\
.SH "SEE ALSO"
\
.MR autoscan 1 ,
.MR renoirpatch 1
\
.SH COPYRIGHT
\
